    "at": "end"
   },
   "cite": "using",
   "prompt": "<p>For the following exercises, determine whether the statement is <em>true or false</em>.</p><p>All vector fields of the form $\\textbf{F}(x,y,z)=f(x)\\textbf{i}+g(y)\\textbf{j}+h(z)\\textbf{k}$ are conservative.</p>",
   "answer": {
    "type": "open",
    "solution": "<p>True, for continuous $f,$ $g$ and $h.$ The cross-partials of $\\textbf{F}=\\langle f(x),g(y),h(z)\\rangle$ are all zero, since each component depends only on its own variable: $P_{y}=Q_{x}=0,$ $P_{z}=R_{x}=0$ and $Q_{z}=R_{y}=0,$ so $\\text{curl}\\;\\textbf{F}=\\mathbf{0}$ on the simply connected domain $\\mathbb{R}^{3}.$ A potential function is $\\varphi(x,y,z)=\\int f(x)\\,dx+\\int g(y)\\,dy+\\int h(z)\\,dz,$ whose gradient is $\\textbf{F}.$</p>",
    "generated_by": "ai"
   }
  },
