   "html": "The $\\mathbf{j}$ and $\\mathbf{k}$ components are printed with the derivatives of the $\\mathbf{i}$ component, $\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}$ and $\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z};$ by the definition of curl they are $\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z}yz-\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}xy=y-y$ and $\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}xz-\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}yz=z-z,$ the values the line gives."
